
  <sn><md>### Chemical Fate of Pollutants

The **chemical fate of a pollutant** refers to the **chemical transformations and changes in form, stability, mobility, and persistence of a pollutant after it enters the environment**.

A pollutant does not always remain in its original chemical form. It may react with **water, oxygen, minerals, organic matter, microorganisms, or other chemicals** and form new substances.

**Main processes controlling chemical fate**

```text
                  POLLUTANT
                      |
          +-----------+-----------+
          |           |           |
     Degradation   Transformation  Reactions
          |           |           |
          v           v           v
   New compounds   New forms    Complexes
          |           |           |
          +-----------+-----------+
                      |
              Changes in pollutant
                      |
        +-------------+-------------+
        |             |             |
     Mobility     Persistence    Toxicity
```

